# {{ .Name }} ({{ .Type }})

Manages the full lifecycle of a KinD cluster: the Docker containers that back
each node, the Kubernetes control plane running inside them, and the kubeconfig
credentials needed to reach it.

~> **Clusters are immutable.** kind cannot add, remove or reconfigure nodes on a
running cluster. Every argument except `wait_for_ready` and
`wait_for_nodes_ready` is marked `RequiresReplace`, so changing one destroys and
recreates the cluster — and everything deployed inside it.

